§ 10-1104 nyc-administrative-code:10-1104 Civil cause of action. Except as otherwise provided by law, any person claiming to be injured by a party who commits, directs, enables, participates in, or conspires in the commission of a crime of violence motivated by gender has a cause of action against such party in any court of competent jurisdiction for any or all of the following relief:

a. Compensatory and punitive damages;

